  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8484;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8484;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Three distinct point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> are randomly chosen from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>. Then the probability that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> form a triangle whose area is a positive integer, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>71</mn><mn>220</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
